@flexiarg math-formalization/weld-range-lemmas-at-representation-seams
@title Weld Range Lemmas at Representation Seams
@keywords Lean, seam, endpoint, periodic, quotient, range, strict, decoding
@audience lean-provers
@tone heuristic
@provenance retro-promotion pass (2026-08-16), source memory e-54ea43ad-bdcf-4c0f-8bf6-2654e14a6ba3

! conclusion:
  At a periodic or quotient representation seam, prove the range statement before
  the endpoint strictly, then prove the endpoint directly from its decoded value.

  + context: A coordinate represents the same geometric point by two boundary
    values, so a closed-endpoint range lemma fails exactly at the wraparound.

  + HOWEVER: First verify the failure is representational. A genuine discontinuity
    or wrong endpoint value cannot be repaired by splitting the proof.

  + THEN: Establish the desired range on the strict pre-end interval; isolate the
    seam point; unfold or simplify its decoder/closed value; combine the two cases.

  + BECAUSE: The strict interval avoids the noncanonical representative while the
    direct endpoint calculation states the quotient identification explicitly.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Locate the exact seam value.]
    next[Prove the strict pre-end range.]
    next[Compute the decoded endpoint directly.]
